  "modified": "2026-10-22T08:53:18Z",
  "details": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: ipv4: raw: reject IP_HDRINCL packets with ihl < 5 (CVE-2026-64114)\n  * kernel: fuse: re-lock request before returning from fuse_ref_folio() (CVE-2026-64266)\n  * kernel: ipv4: fib: free fib_alias with kfree_rcu() on insert error path (CVE-2026-64572)\n  * kernel: ALSA: seq: close a re-opened queue timer in the destructor (CVE-2026-68202)\n  * kernel: xfs: bounds-check buffer log item's dirty bitmap (CVE-2026-80536)\n  * kernel: inet: frags: strip GSO state from fragments before reassembly (CVE-2026-80590)\n  * kernel: vfio/pci: clear vdev->msi_perm after freeing it on init failure (CVE-2026-89777)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
